/* Designer’s notes on Brian Feeney’s items, read through the Game Design Scriptures (the course’s book of design principles).
   These notes are this page’s reading, not Brian’s. lenses: key -> [name, scripture source, what the lens asks]. items: item name -> [lens, note]. types: a note per item type. */
window.FEENEY_NOTES = {"intro":"Each item carries a short designer’s note that reads it through one lens from the Game Design Scriptures, the course’s book of design principles. Pick a lens to see every item that teaches it. The notes are this page’s reading, not Brian’s. Alexander’s Rule of Reverse Justification (Entry 12) warns that a principle quoted after the choice is decoration, so use the lenses as questions when you write your own items: does it add a verb, give the enemy a tell, or change the scene?","lenses":{"tension":["Power with a price","Ortho’s Philosophy of Orthogonal Nuance (Entry 18), Create tension · Scripture of Systems VII.2, Different Things, Equally Valuable","A choice is only interesting when the options pull against each other. These items hand you a strength and a cost in the same sentence."],"loop":["Feedback loop","Ortho’s Philosophy (Entry 18), Tool 8: Feedback loops","An output fed back as an input. Positive loops snowball; negative loops self-correct. Neither is a verdict, they are maths terms."],"fixedness":["A new use for a familiar thing","Scripture of Systems VI.9, Subvert Functional Fixedness","People see objects only in their usual role. Items that reveal a new use for bread, rope or a door make the player feel clever."],"niche":["A job of its own","Ortho’s Philosophy (Entry 18), Niche · Scripture of Systems VII.15, Situational Value","Does it do one job better than anything else? Narrow items vanish in average play and shine when their problem arrives."],"counterplay":["Counterplay and tells","Zileas’s Counterplay Zeitgeist (Entry 17) · Scripture of Systems X.8, Proportional Punishment","Options that beat other options, and threats the opponent can read. The longer and brighter the tell, the bigger the effect can be."],"composition":["One frame, many items","Xelnath’s Compositional Frameworks (Entry 20)","Build a frame once, then fill its slots: the elemental rings, the Marks, the Lantaros and the Soul elixirs are families. If two rows match, it is a reskin."],"versatility":["One verb, many uses","Ortho’s Philosophy (Entry 18), Versatility","Miyamoto’s heuristic: before adding a mechanic, see whether one you have can do the job. One item that answers five problems."],"fantasy":["Fantasy meets mechanic","Alavi Principles for Epic Game Characters (Entry 11) · Scripture of Systems VIII.6, Piggyback","The fiction explains the rule before the rule is read. When the source of power is also the performance, the player lives the fantasy."],"freeform":["Judged by the table","Wagar’s Skill Theorem (Entry 9), Freeform skills","Creativity, communication and humor are hard for rules to score, so these items hand the payoff to the humans at the table."],"synergy":["Setup and payoff","Ortho’s Philosophy (Entry 18), Synergy and Tool 6: Interlocking","Two effects that each work alone and do more together. Many of these items carry their own setup and payoff."],"protect":["Protect the player","Mandos (Entry 4), Protect the Player · Scripture of Systems X.9, Alternate Outcomes","Failure leads somewhere instead of to a dead turn. Safety nets that keep a downed or cornered player in the game."],"information":["Look before you leap","Scripture of Systems VI.3, Variance Generators · Wagar (Entry 9), Input RNG","Information shown before a decision turns a gamble into a puzzle. These items replace guessing with choosing."],"context":["Context sets its value","Scripture of Systems XII.7, The Four Contexts · McEntoss (Entry 3), Context","The same item means different things in water, woods or a library. The level decides how much it matters."],"inversion":["Inversion","Ortho’s Philosophy (Entry 18), Tool 3: Inversion","Write down the assumption and flip it: a torch that sheds darkness, healing that hurts, fear that makes you fast."],"power":["Plain power","Scripture of Systems VII.30, The Price of Power · VII.24, Aesthetic and Hidden Power","A straight boost with no new verb. Fine in moderation, but every power reward costs tension, and the items players retell are rarely these."],"coop":["Only works together","Xelnath’s Cooperative Sequencing Codex (Entry 19)","Strategies that exist only when two players act together: shared stakes, borrowed rolls, rescues and party-only channels."],"distortion":["Pattern breaker","The Way of Nintendo (Entry 16), Distortion of behaviour · Ortho’s Philosophy (Entry 18), Tool 7","A deliberate disruption of the usual pattern that raises the table’s attention, sometimes for the rest of the campaign."],"control":["Player-shaped outcome","Ortho’s Philosophy (Entry 18), Control · McEntoss (Entry 3), Nuance","The player varies the result by input or context: how many charges, which direction, how long to wait."],"randomness":["Randomness on purpose","Scripture of Systems VII.20, Noise, Bounded · Zileas (Entry 17), randomness warnings","Randomness flattens the skill gap and can feel undeserved. These items use it where chaos is the point."],"skill":["A skill test","Wagar’s Skill Theorem (Entry 9)","The item asks the player to perform (a catch, a dance, a turn) and pays out by how well they do."],"exploit":["Playtest for exploits","Scripture of Systems III.8, Mentally Playtest for Exploits · VII.32, Judging Exploits","Walk the optimizer’s path before you hand it out: where does the reward outrun the fun?"]},"types":{"Wondrous":"Wondrous items are the heart of the sheet: 203 of 352, and most change the scene rather than the numbers. Read them for Subvert Functional Fixedness (Scripture of Systems VI.9) and for families built from one frame (the Marks, Baubles and Lantaros; Compositional Frameworks, Entry 20).","Weapon":"Nearly every weapon starts as a +1 and adds one twist. Celia’s depth tiers (Entry 15) separate them: an extra 1d4 grows the possibility space, but a twist that changes how you fight (catch the axe, wait for the fourth shot, swing until the glass snaps) adds differentiated, relevant depth.","Armor":"Brian’s armor treats the plus as the floor and the verb as the reason to wear it. Notice how many trigger at 0 HP (Deathbone, Repose, Mummy, Trollskin): failure leads somewhere instead of to a dead turn (Scripture of Systems X.9, Alternate Outcomes).","Potion":"Players hoard consumables whose replacement cost is unknown (the Hoarder’s Curse, Scripture of Systems III.9). Brian’s potions answer it by being scene-specific: you drink Powder of Unmaking at the door, not ‘someday’. The three Soul elixirs show one frame filled three ways.","Ring":"The five elemental rings share one skeleton (a stat, a defense, two cantrips, a daily spell), and the PentaGauntlet turns them into a collection goal. The Ring of the Betrothed and the Ring of Temptation show a rule-breaker making the original’s rules visible (Scripture of Systems VII.19).","Scroll":"Scrolls here are one-shot rule changes. Decree of Law is the extreme case: it hands the designer’s pen to the player, so the item is only as interesting as the rule they write.","Staff":"Staffs are charge pools with menus. A menu on a shared resource makes every use a choice between this effect now and that one later (the Decision Engine Recipe, Scripture of Systems VI.1).","Wand":"The wands trigger off the enemy’s failures and escalate with repeated hits (Wand of Tears, Wand of Instant Regret), so they reward the party for setting up saves first.","Rod":"Only four rods, and two of them are build-ups: the Slow Cooker grows each round until it explodes, and the Scepter of the Damned Army squares its charges. Steep curves turn spending into a timing decision."},"items":{"Meteor Plate":["tension","Huge burst, but you leave the fight for a full round and must call your landing a turn early. Enemies who read the streak of flame can step out of the circle: a telegraph that pays for the 8d6."],"Toadskin":["counterplay","A reactive answer to melee: it punishes the attacker after they commit, so enemies learn to hit the Toadskin wearer last. The once-per-hour cap keeps it a deterrent rather than a wall."],"Wooly Floof":["fixedness","Padded armor, the weakest armor, becomes a movement tool: falls turn into bounces and hits turn into launches. The fantasy (a sheep surviving a giant's club) explains the rule before the rule is read."],"Bull Hide":["fantasy","One phrase, \"become a bull\", tells the player the speed, the toughness and the charge. Borrowing a creature everyone knows costs almost nothing to teach (piggybacking on existing knowledge)."],"Cavalier's Guard":["fantasy","The summon gesture (jump and spread your legs) is a performance, which turns an action-economy rule into a moment the table laughs at and remembers."],"Deathbone Armor":["protect","Dropping to 0 HP becomes a new phase instead of a dead turn: the player keeps playing as a skeleton. Failure leads somewhere interesting instead of to the sidelines."],"Fungicraft Armor":["synergy","Mirror images that explode when slain ask enemies to choose between wasting attacks and eating poison. Two plain effects interlock into a dilemma."],"Lifesense Heartpiece":["niche","A tiny 5-foot radius makes it a narrow tool: it does nothing in open play and everything in an ambush or a dark corridor. Situational value, not average value."],"Buoyant Armor":["versatility","Float or sink at will answers water, falling, wading and drowning with one verb. One mechanic, many uses."],"Stoneplate":["tension","Stoneskin at the cost of all movement: a pure position-for-defense trade. The player chooses the moment to plant, which is a strategic choice inside a tactical fight."],"Armor of Fangs":["synergy","Rewards grappling, a verb most players ignore, so it pulls a build toward a forgotten part of the rules. Items can shift relevant depth toward unused options."],"Armor of Repose":["protect","Feign death on 0 HP gives a downed player a second chance and gives the table a twist: enemies walk away from someone who is not dead."],"Armor of War":["loop","Temporary HP that refills on each kill is a positive feedback loop: the more you win, the safer you are. \"Honorable combat\" is the brake, and it is a roleplay brake, not a number."],"Stormeye Splint":["tension","At-will Gust of Wind, then a tornado that switches the whole item off until a long rest. The player holds the big button and decides when the fight deserves it."],"Chargemetal Armor":["loop","Absorbing lightning refills the charges, so the item wants you to stand in the enemy's lightning. It turns a threat into a resource, a classic inversion."],"Trollskin Suit":["counterplay","Regeneration with a stated counter (fire or acid), borrowed straight from the troll. Enemies with fire become a priority, which gives the encounter a shape."],"Acoustic Weave":["niche","A support-only multiplier: it does nothing for a Fighter and a lot for a Bard. Narrow items let a class feel its kit grow without power spilling to everyone."],"The Dome":["versatility","A shield becomes terrain. It blocks a corridor, shelters a downed ally or traps an enemy, and the player gives up the shield's AC to do it."],"Kinetic Shield":["loop","Charges come from crits dealt and taken against dangerous foes, so the shield grows strongest in the fights that matter. The DM's call on \"dangerous\" keeps it from being farmed."],"Desert Skin Bracers":["context","A survival item with a combat hook: it matters in the desert and while grappling, and the two contexts share one fantasy (it drinks moisture)."],"Bloodrage Armor":["loop","Each hit hurts more and makes you stronger until combat ends: a deliberate snowball with a self-inflicted cost. It fits the berserker fantasy because the danger is the point."],"Righteous Bear Arms":["fantasy","Golden bear claws plus radiant damage stack two fantasies (beast and holy) into one look. Silhouette and source of power read at once."],"Frozen Shield":["protect","A panic button that costs your turn: you become a block of ice with 50 temporary HP. It trades action for survival, which is the exact choice a cornered player wants."],"Incubi's Vest":["synergy","Charm makes the grapple save fail automatically, so the item contains its own setup and payoff. A two-step combo the player can discover alone."],"Cosmic Hide":["protect","Removing yourself from existence for a turn is a reaction that erases one disaster. The cost (only a move next turn) keeps it a save, not an escape-and-attack."],"Wrappings of the Mummy":["tension","An aura that hurts everyone nearby and blocks their healing, allies included. The player has to position away from friends, which turns a buff into a team puzzle."],"Ropeplate":["versatility","Entangle, grapple and climbing from one coil of rope. Combat and traversal share a verb, so the item never sits idle."],"Plated Superarmor":["tension","+4 Strength for -10 speed is a stat trade players can feel. The extra gauntlets add a playful verb (hold more things) on top of the numbers."],"Flaerrinton's Mercurial Solution":["exploit","Duplicating any potion asks \"what is the most valuable potion in this world?\" and the answer sets this item's real power. Mentally playtest the optimizer's path before handing it out."],"Odh's Green Tea":["context","Plant Growth that ignores your allies makes the terrain itself pick sides. It is strongest where there are plants, so the level decides how much it matters."],"Elixir of Magic Resistance":["niche","An anti-magic field on one person is a hard counter: it shuts off magic both ways. Hard counters belong on consumables, where they are rare and chosen."],"Bottled Lightning":["fantasy","A short, readable power spike: you are lightning for a minute. Bottled names teach the effect before the rules do."],"Sensual Slippery Soap":["tension","Advantage on Dex saves and Persuasion, but anyone tracking you smells you coming. Every strength carries an exploitable weakness, written right into the joke."],"Powder of Unmaking":["fixedness","Unmaking works on doors, chains, weapons and food, so the player looks at every object as a recipe. It rewards creativity rather than a stat."],"Soldier Serum":["tension","Brawn for brains, and the third use makes it permanent. A slow-burn temptation that turns a consumable into a character decision."],"Soul of the Arbiter":["composition","One of three Soul elixirs: the same template (a new class, new stats, a new alignment, a temp-HP fuse) with different contents. Build one frame, ship three items."],"Soul of the Savage":["fantasy","You play a different character for a day, with an urge the player must roleplay. The mechanic makes the player feel the marauder's dilemma."],"Soul of the Champion":["composition","Read the three Soul elixirs side by side: the frame stays fixed and only the class and stats change. Variants are cheap and need little teaching once the first is known."],"Elixir of Profuse Sweating":["versatility","A gross joke with three real uses: fire, cold and grapple escapes. Humor makes the rules memorable."],"God's Healing Elixir":["tension","Massive healing that punishes you for overhealing. The player has to time it, so a healing potion becomes a decision instead of a reflex."],"Animal Snax":["fixedness","Treats make a beast into a temporary party member. It hands non-Druids a taste of animal companionship for one scene."],"Sphere of Insanity":["randomness","A body-swap lottery for everyone within 150 feet, friends included. Use randomness on purpose: this one is a scene-ending chaos bomb, so it belongs in the DM's hands or a desperate moment."],"Bear Claw":["composition","Two modes in one pastry (hybrid or dire bear) and no early exit unless you throw up. The joke is the off switch."],"Bloodhound Juice":["information","Tracking a single target across a mile turns a manhunt into a direction. Information items convert guesswork into choices."],"Potion of Extreme Belching":["versatility","Pushes enemies and the drinker at the same time, so it is an escape, a shove off a ledge and a gag. Knockback both ways makes positioning matter."],"Zombification":["inversion","Healing hurts and necrotic heals: one rule flip turns your Cleric into the threat and the enemy Necromancer into a medic. Inversion creates a new puzzle from known rules."],"Elixir of Death":["fixedness","Death as a tool: fake your death, skip a poison, slip past a guard. A downside item that clever players turn into an upside."],"Pain Reducer":["protect","Spreads burst damage across rounds so you can't be one-shot, then charges exhaustion. It smooths spikes rather than adding health, a different shape of defense."],"Ring of Arrow Deflection":["synergy","Missed arrows bounce into enemies near you, so you want to stand next to foes while archers shoot at you. The item rewrites where you should stand."],"Cantrip Focus Ring":["niche","A sorcerer cantrip for anyone, a power-up for a Sorcerer. The same item has two readings depending on who holds it."],"Ring of Spell Absorption":["counterplay","A reaction that drags enemy spells onto you, then eats them on a big fail. It is a protector's tool: it moves danger off the fragile ally."],"Ring of Undying Fury":["tension","Extra damage plus a death save that gets harder as the hits get bigger. The ring dies with you, so using it is a commitment."],"Fey Spirit Ring":["loop","You catch fey spirits mid-combat to grow the ring, so the item creates a side objective in every fight. Its menu (reveal, vanish, swap places, release) gives each charge a choice."],"The Resilience of Earth":["composition","The first of five elemental rings: each sets one stat to 18, adds a defense, two cantrips and a daily spell. A clear skeleton (stat, defense, cantrips, signature) makes the family easy to read and extend."],"The Fury of Flame":["composition","Fury of Flame fills the same slots as its siblings with fire. When two rows of a composition table match, it is a reskin; here the stat and signature spell differ, so each ring plays differently."],"The Grace of Air":["composition","Grace of Air: Dexterity, Evasion, initiative and flight. Each elemental ring answers a different problem (survive, hit, dodge, breathe, sense)."],"The Serenity of Water":["composition","Serenity of Water carries two stats and proficiency in every save, the broadest ring of the five. Check whether it outclasses its siblings: one dominant option collapses the choice."],"The Eternity of Spirit":["composition","Eternity of Spirit is the social ring: telepathy, mockery and True Seeing. It gives the Charisma player a combat-light identity inside a combat-heavy family."],"Ring of Fireflies":["tension","Light and an early warning, but you glow. Visibility as the price of information is a clean trade."],"Ring of Reasonable Wishes":["tension","Wishes with a ceiling (a 5th-level caster) turn \"I wish\" from a rules lawyer's dream into a creative prompt. The limit is what makes the wish interesting."],"Ring of Retrieval":["protect","Recall your gear as a bonus action: it defuses the \"you wake up in a cell, unarmed\" scene and every disarm. Protect players from setbacks that feel arbitrary."],"Ring of the Betrothed":["coop","A ring that only works in pairs and curses both when the bond breaks. A strategy that exists only together, with a shared stake."],"Ring of Temptation":["counterplay","A trap built on its sibling: it looks like a Ring of the Betrothed and steals the bond. A rule-breaker that makes the original's rules visible, and a hook for a betrayal story."],"Riding Whistle":["fantasy","A whistle that calls your horse across a mile delivers a fantasy every rider wants. Small conveniences can carry big identity."],"Ring of the Mother Spider":["coop","Bound wearers share climbing and a protective web. It rewards staying close and gives one player a way to guard another without being there."],"Scepter of the Damned Army":["loop","Undead squared by charges (1, 4, 9 ... 100) makes the last charge worth far more than the first, so the player is tempted to save up. A steep curve on a slow recharge turns into a hoarding decision."],"Slow Cooker":["tension","Damage grows every round you keep firing, then explodes on you if you push past the cap. A build-up with a cliff edge: the player has to stop at the right moment."],"Multitool":["versatility","Every reusable tool in three kits, in one rod. It removes inventory friction so the table spends time on choices, not packing lists."],"Rod of Electrical Control":["control","Puppet an enemy with a rod: you steer their movement and attacks, and each forced action gives them a save. A strong effect with a built-in exit."],"Scroll of Magic for Dunces":["niche","A borrowed cantrip for a day lets a non-caster try magic. It is a sampler, and samplers teach players what they might want next."],"Note of Repayment":["tension","Pay with a promise and the debt comes back with a face. A short-term win becomes a future plot hook: the item writes story."],"Martial Technique":["niche","Lends a Battlemaster maneuver for an hour, so any character can try a tactical move once. It teaches a system by letting players taste it."],"Autocartrographer":["information","An auto-filling map removes the busywork of mapping without removing exploration. Make it easier before trying to make people care more."],"Trivial Scroll":["information","Answers one question about a non-living thing. The constraint shapes the question, and choosing the question is the game."],"Infiniscroll":["fixedness","Infinite paper sounds useless until players use it for bridges, kindling, signals or a paper fortress. Infinity of a mundane thing invites creativity."],"Siphoning Scroll":["counterplay","Steals an enemy's scroll mid-cast. Reactive counters reward players who watch the opponent and hold their reaction."],"Ninja Scroll":["distortion","A scroll that stabs: once players learn it exists, every scroll pile becomes suspicious. A single surprise raises attention for the rest of the campaign."],"Decree of Law":["control","The player writes the rule and every enemy who breaks it takes damage. A designer's tool handed to a player: it is only as interesting as the rule they choose."],"Scroll of Repetition":["synergy","Everything that happens to the target happens again, helpful or harmful. It turns the next ally's turn into the payoff, a setup that the whole party exploits."],"The Nope Stick":["fixedness","Three shouted commands map to three conditions (silence, blind, immobilize). The joke (\"Shut up!\") is the user interface: the player remembers the effect by the phrase."],"Staff of the Storm":["versatility","One charge pool, three spends (on-hit damage, chain lightning with a teleport, Lightning Bolt). A menu on a shared resource creates a choice every time you use it."],"Staff of Hail":["tension","A sleet storm around you that never touches you, so you fight inside your own zone. It asks the party to bring the fight to you."],"Pitfall Shovel":["versatility","Holes are traps, cover, graves, escape tunnels and pits for enemies. Burying the shovel to recharge it is a wink that rewards the player for playing along."],"Oaken Staff of the Treant":["fantasy","A staff that becomes a tree and wakes the plants. The recharge doubles outdoors, so the item asks to be used where its fantasy belongs."],"Staff of Snakes":["tension","Turning an enemy's limb into a snake is a permanent, story-scale effect. Effects that outlast the fight are expensive, and the charge cost reflects that."],"Wand of Instant Regret":["synergy","Punishes failed rolls and natural 1s, so it pairs with anything that forces saves. The wand turns other players' setups into your payoff."],"Wand of Hidden Truths":["freeform","A wand whose result is a sentence the DM decides. Freeform effects can't be scored by rules, so they hand the payoff to the humans at the table."],"Wand of the Glutton":["fixedness","Finishing an enemy by turning it into food is a kill effect with personality. A damage spell becomes a joke the party retells."],"Wand of Nightmares":["synergy","Sleep, then nightmares, then an illusion with disadvantage: one wand holds its own setup, exploit and payoff. The order of charges is the skill."],"Wand of Tears":["loop","Each hit deepens the crying (disadvantage, then half speed, then immobilized), but any damage ends it. The player must choose between escalating the control and dealing damage."],"Pitchfork of Revolution":["context","Mass Suggestion that only works when it points toward revolution. The item has an opinion, and the world's politics decide its power."],"Blade of Alarm":["information","It screams when a hostile is near, so nobody needs to roll Perception. It removes a roll rather than adding to one."],"Scythe of the Damned":["loop","Every kill gives you a one-turn ally. Strong in big fights, quiet in duels: the item scales with the number of enemies."],"Vinelash":["niche","One effect, reach of 30 feet, and nothing else. Simple items leave room for players to find the uses (pull a lever, grab a falling ally)."],"Chef Knife":["fantasy","It cooks what it cuts, enemies included. A tiny damage bonus delivered with a smell: aesthetic power the table remembers."],"Stilleto of Possession":["tension","You take the body of whatever you kill and leave your own behind. A power so large that using it is a story decision, not a combat one."],"Fork of Furious Stabbing":["loop","The fork grows from a d2 to 2d8 as you keep landing hits, and the color changes with it. Visible power growth inside one fight makes the player feel the snowball."],"Butcher's Knife":["loop","Kills chain into free attacks. It rewards finishing wounded enemies first, which tells the player how to target."],"Portal Bow":["control","Teleport where you shoot, and a miss scatters you by how far you missed. Skill (the attack roll) shapes the outcome by degree, not pass or fail."],"Bolts of Madness":["randomness","A berserk target attacks the nearest unit, friend or foe. Your positioning decides whether the chaos helps you."],"Boltsurge Crossbow":["loop","Kills refund charges, so a well-timed big shot pays for the next one. A positive loop with a natural limit (the number of enemies)."],"Blades of the Huntsman":["information","Three knives you can always locate turn a weapon into a tracking device. Slip one into a pocket and the hunt is on."],"Tordle's Explosive Mushrooms":["counterplay","Mines stuck to a square: the danger is visible once spotted, and enemies must choose their path. Placed threats create space control."],"Dart's of Eternal Love":["loop","Each extra dart makes the charm harder to shake. A stacking effect rewards focus fire."],"Mageseeker's Talon":["counterplay","Charges come from enemy spells, then spend against casters. A weapon that is strongest exactly against what it hunts, the Mageseeker fantasy written as rules."],"Glacialfreeze Bow":["loop","Stacking slows that shatter at zero speed: a visible countdown both sides can read. Building to a payoff gives the archer a plan, not just damage."],"The Party Whip":["niche","A one-round dance that each creature can fail only once a day. The limit keeps a hilarious lockdown from becoming a permanent one."],"Duelists' Blade":["tension","Skip your attack for AC and a counterattack on near misses. The parry fantasy as a choice between offense and defense."],"Showman's Axe":["skill","Catch your own axe with an Acrobatics check to power the next throw. The source of power is also the performance (the Draven pattern): the player shows off to get stronger."],"Soul Render's Grasp":["tension","Pull out the enemy's spirit and tether it: damage the spirit to hurt the body, or force the enemy to break the tether and take a curse. Leaving the enemy two costly options is what makes it strong."],"Dwarven Handcannon of Patience":["tension","The fourth shot is huge, but if you wait too long the crossbow explodes. Patience is rewarded until it isn't, so the player watches a timer."],"Echo Wraps":["niche","Blindsense after each unarmed hit is a small, specific answer to invisible enemies and darkness. Narrow tools stand out when the right problem shows up."],"Blade of Radiance":["information","Light and Faerie Fire on hit reveal hidden enemies. The item answers darkness and invisibility for the whole party."],"Hammers of Light":["inversion","A weapon that can heal, thrown at an ally who lowers their shield to receive it. Inverting the target turns an attack roll into a teamwork moment."],"Hunting Blade":["niche","Hunter's Mark for anyone who carries the blade. Borrowing a class feature spreads a ranger's identity to a fighter for a fight."],"The PentaGauntlet":["composition","The capstone of the elemental ring family: collect all five and they become at-will. A collection goal turns five items into a long-term quest."],"Knife of Wind":["versatility","Damage, a 5-foot push and free movement in one knife. Mobility items keep the player's damage capability above zero."],"Axe of Lightning":["niche","Chain damage to a second enemy rewards fighting in crowds. It tells the player where to stand."],"The Storm Herald":["composition","Three earlier items combine into one. A crafting goal written into the item list, and a reason to keep the parts."],"Winged Arrows":["fixedness","An arrow that drags whatever it is tied to: rope, ally, enemy or loot. A ranged attack becomes a traversal and rescue tool."],"Crystalline Sling":["tension","Gems explode by type, and each gem can be used only once. Treasure becomes ammunition, so the player weighs gold against power."],"Devastating Bottle":["tension","One stunning hit, then it becomes a broken-bottle scimitar. The weapon's state changes as you use it, a story told in two acts."],"Golden Knuckles of Freedom":["fantasy","Coins fly from struck enemies, and pocketing them breaks the knuckles forever. The rule enforces the character's code, so the player has to live the fantasy."],"Shockstick":["versatility","Three supercharges spend on damage or on reviving a downed ally. A shared pool between offense and rescue creates a real choice mid-fight."],"Crow Bar":["loop","Each hit adds a crow, and the flock keeps pecking. A visible swarm that grows with persistence."],"Boulder of Surprise":["fixedness","A pebble that becomes a boulder: damage, a wall, a roadblock or a door stop. The command word means it can be undone, so it is a toolbox, not a one-shot."],"Injector":["coop","Fires potions into allies or poisons into enemies. The targeting matrix in one weapon: the same shot means healing or harm depending on who it hits."],"Traitor's Blade":["tension","Auto-crit against anyone who doesn't see you as hostile. The weapon rewards betrayal, which makes trust a resource at the table."],"Terrorhook":["fantasy","The weapon becomes the target's worst fear. The look is the mechanic: the player describes the fear and the fright follows."],"Quipper Needler":["context","Fires underwater and stacks bleeding. Strong in one environment, ordinary elsewhere, which gives an aquatic campaign its own weapon."],"Shark Cannon":["fantasy","A crossbow that fires sharks, and the sharks flop slowly on land. The rule for \"on land\" keeps the joke honest and the power tied to its environment."],"Curse Eater":["inversion","Removing a curse powers the weapon with necrotic damage. The holy act feeds a dark edge, a contradiction that makes the item a character."],"Skylancers Pike":["control","Spend any number of charges for reach and damage this round. The player sets the size of the spike, and saving charges is a choice."],"Flourishing Rapier":["synergy","Disarm, then hit them with their own weapon. The payoff is built into the setup, and it is the kind of move players tell stories about."],"Hookboots":["versatility","Weapons on your feet that also help you climb. Monk-friendly and traversal-friendly in one slot."],"Fang of Corruption":["tension","Unhealable necrotic damage and an at-will spray, but animals flee you and plants die where you walk. The wyrm-and-lich fantasy carries a social cost every day."],"Arm of DarkIce":["synergy","Auto-crits on full-health enemies, freezes the dead and shatters them into a cone. The opening hit and the finishing blow both have a job, so the fight has a shape."],"Spiked Tail of Inferno":["synergy","Fire damage grows with every tile or creature already burning. It rewards setting the battlefield alight first, a setup and payoff in one whip."],"Claw of Venom":["control","Switch venoms as a bonus action, and the Deadly venom kills only after two others land. A venom menu turns each hit into sequencing."],"Horn of Storm":["counterplay","Mark a target, and lightning strikes it at the start of your next turn. A delayed strike gives the enemy a tell and you a prediction game."],"Warpstar":["niche","Short teleports that keep you in reach turn a slow weapon into a sticky one. Movement keeps a melee character's damage capability above zero."],"Club of Celebratation":["coop","Kills and crits inspire everyone nearby. One player's moment of glory becomes a shared success."],"Spellcleaver":["synergy","Casting a spell charges the next swing, so the item asks a hybrid to alternate. It gives the gish fantasy a rhythm."],"Mirageblade":["distortion","Advantage only against foes who haven't seen it or been hit by it. It is strongest on the first strike, which makes the ambush the plan."],"Flail of Arcane Vampirism":["counterplay","Turn off an enemy's magic item, then once a day keep its power yourself. It answers gear-heavy foes and makes looting a mid-fight action."],"Wilting Flower":["counterplay","Wilt the enemy's weapon to half damage for a day, then the whip rests. A strong debuff with a clear cost: one use per dawn."],"Arm of God":["fantasy","A prosthetic god-arm that only fits someone missing an arm. The restriction is a story requirement, and it turns an injury into a destiny."],"Omniglaive":["loop","Charges build with each hit, then spend in a flurry across nearby enemies, at the cost of exhaustion. Build-up and release, Electricity in Rogers' feel terms."],"Greatsword of Glass":["tension","Huge damage that drains with every hit until the blade snaps. A visible countdown makes every swing count."],"Torvald's Brain Jar":["information","Watch the last 30 seconds of a death. A mystery engine: it answers \"how\" and leaves \"why\" for the players."],"Globe of Goblin Insight":["freeform","Divination answered by an Int 9 goblin. The comedy is in the gap between the question and the answer, and the DM gets to play it."],"Malleable Ingot":["versatility","A bar of iron that becomes whatever you need, any number of times. Open-ended items reward the players who think in shapes."],"Arsonist's Torch":["context","Everything flammable around you catches fire. The room decides the danger, so the same torch is a light in a cave and a disaster in a library."],"Shadow Torch":["inversion","Light only you can see: a torch for stealth. Inverting who benefits from light gives the rogue a new tool."],"Twinevine":["versatility","Endless rope, up to 50 feet a day, that crumbles after a week. Cheap to use, so players use it often: the opposite of the hoarded consumable."],"Manacles of Honorable Combat":["coop","Lock two combatants into a duel. A fighter can pin the enemy champion so the rest of the party handles the crowd."],"Glow Torch":["information","Lights up every living creature nearby, invisible ones included. An answer to invisibility that also gives away your allies."],"(Language) Bifocals":["niche","Read text from 30 feet away or in any language up close. A puzzle-solving tool that changes how the DM writes clues."],"Charming Monocle":["tension","Charm with a wink, but a failed charm bounces back on you. The backfire risk turns a free action into a gamble."],"Onyx Pendant":["information","It buzzes near undead and does nothing else. One-line items teach the DM to seed a mystery around them."],"Badge of Authority":["fixedness","A disguise as a local guard turns a fight at the gate into a con. It moves the scene from combat to social."],"Goblin Sniffer":["composition","A goblin nose that comes in giant, orc and kobold varieties. A variant family built from one template."],"Prismatic Goggles":["counterplay","Chaos Bolts that fire elements in a fixed order. Players learn the cycle, so randomness becomes a pattern they can plan around."],"Bangle of Invisibility":["fixedness","Invisible, but only one limb. A small power that rewards creative uses: pickpocketing, sleight of hand, a ghostly wave."],"Bowtie of Swagger":["skill","Blur that lasts as long as you keep dancing, with the DC rising each round. A skill test that escalates until you choose to stop."],"Oak Beehive":["tension","Honey every day, bees on demand, and a swarm if you drop it. The item is useful, and it is also a hazard to carry."],"Hexbag":["counterplay","Plant it on someone and everyone who attacks them hexes them. They can find it, which gives the victim a way out."],"Malekin's Magnificent Egg":["freeform","Hatch a tiny version of whatever's blood you sprinkle on it. A pet generator: the value is the story, not the stats."],"Boots of Animal Tracks":["fixedness","Fake animal tracks turn pursuit into misdirection. A tracking puzzle for the enemy instead of the party."],"Lamp of Distraction":["niche","A lamp that enthralls onlookers. A distraction tool that buys time for a heist."],"Pillow of Wonderful Dreams":["randomness","Faster rest plus a chance of visions, nightmares or false prophecies. The DM gets a hook for plot hints with a built-in fog of doubt."],"Boots of Reversed Momentum":["control","Launches you 30 feet backward from the way you last moved. The player sets up the direction first, a small skill puzzle in movement."],"Magnetic Boots":["tension","Lock in place and nobody can move you, but you can't move either. Choosing when to plant is the decision."],"Gloves of Greed":["versatility","Steal coins in a cone. Funny at a market, strong in a heist, and a cause of trouble when it pulls from the wrong pocket."],"Cloak of Beetles":["fantasy","Turn into a swarm of beetles. A shapeshift that gives escape, scouting and squeezing through gaps."],"Torch of the Abyss":["inversion","A torch that sheds darkness instead of light. Inverting the most common item in the game produces a new tool for ambushes."],"Tag of Recall":["protect","Tag an item and it returns after a set time. A failsafe against theft, and a delayed-delivery trick."],"Ladle of the Frosted Peak":["fixedness","A ladle with three histories: a giant's treat, halfling ice cream, frozen slingstones. Brian writes the uses into the lore, which teaches players to invent their own."],"Robe of the Moon":["composition","A robe with four phases, each with its own teleport and bonus. The moon gives the item a schedule, and the player plans around it."],"Oven Gloves":["inversion","Inside, the gloves burn; turned inside out they protect. The same object holds both sides of a rule."],"Performers Mask":["composition","Masks that fuse into a set, each with a skill and a command. Collecting them grows the menu, and the DC grows with the set."],"Robe of Scrolls":["versatility","A wardrobe of utility spells that refill weekly. Many small options, chosen in the moment."],"Bearded Helmet":["fantasy","Grow a beard, become a dwarf. The bonus arrives over days of play, and the lore warns of believing it too much."],"Bracers of the Wolf":["protect","AC for unarmored characters and two wolves on demand. A dependable item that raises the floor."],"Demon Eyes":["counterplay","Sees through celestial and fey illusions and hits celestials harder. One half of a mirrored pair, each counters the other's maker."],"Angel Eyes":["counterplay","The mirror of Demon Eyes: sees through fiendish and fey illusions and hits fiends harder. Mirrored items make the opposing rules visible."],"Belt of Quickdraw":["power","+2 initiative and a free draw. A plain stat item, and that is fine: not every item needs a new verb, but the ones that add one are remembered."],"Belt of Extreme Size Differential":["fantasy","Enlarge yourself and shrink everyone nearby, with a two-inch vanity effect always on. The constant joke advertises the big effect."],"Bodybag":["niche","A bag of holding for corpses only, and they don't decay. A specific item that gives the party a specific errand."],"Paint of the Beast":["context","Speak with one type of animal for an hour. A social tool that changes value with the environment."],"Collar of Tiny Reanimation":["fantasy","A lich's collar for a lost pet. The origin story is the emotional hook, and the mechanic follows from it."],"Steelgrate Gills":["context","Breathe any liquid for an hour a day. It matters only where liquid matters, which gives the DM a reason to build that place."],"Stocking of Stretching":["fantasy","Stretchy socks for climbing and jumping. A silly image that players remember better than \"+5 Athletics\"."],"Lover's Earrings":["coop","Two-way whispers between two players. A communication tool that only works when shared."],"Guardian's Bandages":["coop","Pull a downed ally to you and stabilize them. A rescue verb: the player gets a moment of glory by saving someone."],"Dominator's Bandages":["tension","Three saves for three effects (immobilize, pull, crush), once a day. The layered saves make it reliable without being certain."],"Riftwalk Greaves":["tension","Teleport, kick, repeat, with each use in a combat costing more. A rising cost limits spam without a hard cap."],"Infernal Dino Guardian":["fantasy","A stuffed dino that becomes a fire-breathing Allosaurus. The reveal is the reward."],"Mark of Combustion":["counterplay","A one-minute fuse: strong if they don't know, survivable if they do. Unaware creatures save with disadvantage, so information is the multiplier."],"Mark of Vines":["composition","The Mark family shares a template: activate, wait one minute, then an effect. Combustion, Vines, Teleportation, Thievery and Flight each fill the same slot with a different payload."],"Mark of Teleportation":["randomness","A random destination 300 feet away, so the effect is a removal, not a placement. Random output works here because the goal is \"anywhere but here\"."],"Tiny Iron Mark-et":["randomness","Pay 500 gold for a random Mark. A gacha box in a fantasy shop: the price is fixed, the contents are not, and every Mark in the pool is useful, so no pull is a dud."],"Mark of Thievery":["counterplay","Strip a creature of every possession after a one-minute fuse. A heist tool that rewards planning and punishes the unwary."],"Prismatic Torch":["counterplay","A blinding flash that aware allies resist more easily. Warning your own party is part of using it, which builds a callout habit."],"Bardic Journal":["freeform","The illusion uses the reader's own imagination. Pure flavor, and a lovely prop for a storytelling table."],"Mark of Dangerous Flight":["composition","Another Mark: same fuse, same unaware-disadvantage, new payload (launch 80 feet up). Fixing the frame makes each new Mark cheap to learn."],"Amulet of Banishment":["niche","A bonus against three creature types and Turn Undead for more foes. Narrow items shine in a campaign built around their targets."],"Arcane Fragmenter":["synergy","A floating crystal that splits single-target spells across everyone near it. It turns a wizard's single-target list into area effects, but the crystal can be destroyed."],"Portable Window":["information","See through a wall without being seen, and once a week step through it. Look before you commit: information that turns an ambush into a plan."],"Stunning Robe":["power","+1 to spell saves and a daily stun on a shouted spell. A simple boost with a fun trigger (yell the words)."],"Comet of Ruin":["control","A rock orbiting two tiles clockwise each turn. Its position is predictable, so players learn to walk enemies into its path."],"Blanket of Slumber":["versatility","Faster rest or a sleep spell when thrown over someone. The same blanket is camp gear and a kidnapping tool."],"Merfolk Girdle":["context","A tail underwater and a portable cube of water on land. The second effect brings the environment with you."],"Bandana of Cowardice":["inversion","You become frightened, and fear makes you fast. The condition players usually avoid becomes a getaway engine."],"Skeleton Key of Ownership":["fixedness","The key convinces people you own the place. A lockpick becomes a social tool, and a break-in becomes a role-play scene."],"Rat Tail":["fixedness","Stick it on someone and they become a rat. A polymorph with a sense of humor and a stealth use."],"Flamespitter Mask":["power","A fire cone each turn for a minute. A straightforward damage item with a strong look."],"Emerald Snugg":["loop","A turtle that eats coins and sheds a gem. It converts small change into one valuable item, and its hunger can cause trouble at the wrong moment."],"Gloves of the Mime":["versatility","Mime a wall, a pull, a ladder or a barrier: four effects from one fantasy. The gestures are the interface, so players remember them."],"Farsight Crystal":["tension","Five times the range, but only prone and with a full-round action. A sniper's trade of mobility for reach."],"Inferno Cart":["skill","A rocket cart with a turning check and fuel costs. It adds a driving minigame to a tabletop, and wipeouts are part of the fun."],"Facial Razor":["inversion","One edge removes hair, the other grows it. Two sides of one tool."],"Tarrasque Paper":["niche","Paper that can't be destroyed by mundane means. A tiny item that protects the wizard's most important possession."],"Harnait's Overnight Forest":["context","Plant a forest overnight, native to the terrain. It reshapes the map, so it is a strategic tool more than a combat one."],"Stonecutter's Handbook":["loop","Pay yearly to belong, and your gold flows to the next believer. A pyramid scheme as a magic item, and a satire with rules."],"Stormboard":["versatility","A hoverboard with speed, attack-of-opportunity protection and feather fall. Movement items compound: each bonus makes the others more useful."],"Surgepack":["synergy","Bolts onto a weapon or onto the Stormboard. An add-on that rewards owning a specific other item."],"Headband of Excessive Beauty":["fantasy","Charisma, initiative and four social skills, but only once your hair grows in. The delay is a joke that makes the item feel earned."],"Paint of Wonder":["freeform","Endless paint in any color. A creativity tool with no combat use."],"Bonfire of Revival":["protect","If someone dies nearby, you burn and come back. A self-revive on a timer, with a dramatic animation built in."],"Medallion of Eternal Glory":["loop","A medallion that upgrades through six tiers as you slay bigger foes. A progression track inside one item, with a social pecking order on top."],"Flutterwings":["niche","Wings for a familiar. Support gear for the pet, not the player."],"Handkerchief of Misery":["fixedness","Make someone cry until they leave, unless combat starts. A non-violent removal tool."],"Ponaise Disturbing Servant":["distortion","A servant that moves only when no one is watching. The rule changes how players look around a room, a pattern break borrowed from horror."],"Extremely Absorbent Cloak":["fixedness","A cloak that holds 100 gallons. Floods, fires and drowning rooms all have a new answer."],"Scouts Eye":["information","An eye you throw into the sky for a scout's view. Scouting turns a blind approach into a plan."],"Shock Choker":["tension","A shock collar for prisoners, or for a party member. An item that invites table drama; use it with care."],"Eyebrows of Excessive Expressiveness":["niche","Everyone understands you through your eyebrows. A language solution with a gag attached."],"Sash of Focus":["niche","Unarmed damage for anyone, levels for a Monk. Two readings depending on who holds it."],"Orb of Seasons":["context","Change the season for a mile. A campaign-scale lever that affects travel, crops and enemies."],"JibJab's Instant Staircase":["fixedness","A 2-inch staircase that grows to 20 feet. A bridge, a ramp, a wall: players see a staircase and find six uses."],"Slowsand":["tension","Lose 1d4 turns, but nobody can touch you. A removal that also protects the victim, so it buys time, not kills."],"Bracers of Incredible Confidence":["power","Proficiency with any weapon plus involuntary flourishes. A wide stat boost wearing a personality."],"Saltstick":["loop","Each failed roll stings again, and it stacks. It punishes enemies for missing, which favors defensive allies."],"Tombstone of Eternal Remembrance":["information","Ask the dead questions daily until the spirit gets annoyed. The limit is in-fiction, so the cap is funny instead of arbitrary."],"Greedsbane":["counterplay","A coin that punishes thieves by making all their money heavy. A deterrent, not a weapon."],"Flag of Incredibly Victory":["tension","Aid and Bless for everyone, until an enemy breaks it and casts Bane on your army. A banner that becomes a target, a classic risk-reward object."],"Chest of Glorious Battle":["composition","A mini-game inside the game: pick a premade class and fight in an arena. A whole ruleset in one item, built from familiar class archetypes."],"Toxin Mask":["loop","While poisoned, you spit poison. It turns a condition into a weapon."],"Irresistible Spices":["distortion","Season an enemy and their allies try to eat them. A combat-scramble item that flips the battlefield."],"Skull of Servitude":["loop","A zombie from any headless body, with charges lost when it dies. A minion that costs you when you spend it carelessly."],"Accordian of Discomfort":["tension","Make a target itch until they strip their armor. A comic debuff with real tactical value."],"Slippers and Tassels of Epic Dancing":["niche","Dance instead of using somatic components. A bard-specific tool that changes how the class plays."],"Flute of Inspiration":["niche","Bigger dice for bards, a taste of inspiration for others. A support item that scales with who holds it."],"Bagpipes of Distraction":["inversion","Turn inspiration into a penalty on enemies. The same die, flipped in sign."],"Band of the Dance":["skill","Dance to unlock full Jack of All Trades. A performance check as the gate to power."],"Augmented Armbelt":["power","An extra arm that holds things and makes free attacks. Raw action economy, the strongest kind of power in 5e."],"Cowl of Silence":["coop","Allies can use your Stealth roll instead of their own. Four rolls become one, which moves the scene's spotlight to the item's owner."],"Amulet of the Warmaster":["niche","Bigger dice and a swappable maneuver for a Battlemaster. A deepening item for one class."],"Boots of Water Mastery":["synergy","Flood the area, then steam or freeze everyone touching the water. A setup and two payoffs on one charge pool."],"Crown of Knowledge's Burden":["tension","Read anything, but unread books attack you. A strong item with a funny cost that keeps libraries interesting."],"Scabbard of Flames":["power","Flaming blade for a minute, with a spark of lightning on the draw. A clean, readable boost."],"Shawl of Doves":["protect","+1 saves, doves for persuasion, a daily blinding flock. A defensive item that also performs."],"Siphoning Manacles":["loop","A slow life drain between two creatures. The rate (1 HP per minute) makes it a torture or ritual tool, not a combat one."],"Supporting Structure":["protect","A stool that catches falls and prevents prone. Protecting players from small errors, as Mandos asks."],"Weapon of Mass Destruction":["niche","Triple damage to objects and knockback on crits. The item finds its moment on doors, walls and siege."],"Augmentation Kit":["versatility","Add one property to up to three weapons. A crafting system in a box."],"Blowgun":["power","Double range and a Gust of Wind per minute. A blowgun turned into a battlefield control tool."],"Super Fungi":["freeform","A charismatic mushroom person who loves high fives. An NPC in a pocket."],"Shimmercloak":["coop","Make an ally invisible as long as they stay adjacent. It forces two players to move as one."],"Medallion of Impeccable Courage":["context","+1 to hit per size larger, -1 per size smaller. A giant-slayer's tool that fails against small things."],"Cloak of the Swamp Hag":["versatility","Swim through mud, a stench stun and ugly illusions. A swamp kit in one cloak."],"Memory Bead":["information","Transfer a memory into a bead. A storytelling device that delivers lore or clues."],"Experience Bead":["composition","A variant of the Memory Bead that grants skills instead of memories. Variants teach themselves once you know the original."],"Shepard's Knapsack":["niche","A bag of holding for animals with a pond inside. A pet-carrier that opens stealth and smuggling scenes."],"Nobberosh's Correction Apparatus":["protect","An apparatus that hurts you to free you from conditions. It trades HP for agency, which most players will take."],"Tanglefoot's Scrumptious Edibles":["synergy","Turns a long potion into seven tiny one-round bites. It reshapes a consumable's timing, which is its own kind of power."],"Liquid Ink":["freeform","Shape-shifting tattoos. A pure expression item."],"Buttery Mail":["fixedness","Mail delivered by a buttered envelope. A message system with a sound effect."],"Brand of Communal Judgement":["freeform","A curse that makes people rate their interactions with you. A satire of review culture written as rules, and the table judges the result."],"Wheels of Perpetual Motion":["fixedness","Wheels that force movement: strap them on an enemy and walk them off a ledge, or on yourself for a free 10 feet. A movement buff that doubles as a trap."],"Iron Turtle":["protect","A thrown turtle that blocks an attack on an ally, then waddles back. A protector's reaction with a slow, funny return trip."],"Scrollwheel":["power","Two scrolls in one action. Action economy is the strongest currency in 5e, so this small bracer is quietly one of the strongest items here."],"Wings of Knowledge":["loop","Wings that burn down as you fly and refuel on used scrolls. A resource that shrinks visibly, so flight time is a decision."],"Feather of Authenticity":["freeform","A perfect signature and invisible magic ink. A forger's and spy's tool, valued by the plot rather than the rules."],"Lantaro of Introduction":["composition","The Lantaro family: six orbs, each +1 to one stat, each with a personality and one verb. A frame (stat, personality, verb, fragility) that makes a set of companions."],"Lantaro of Beratement":["composition","Beratement: the Intelligence orb insults a foe and deals psychic damage when they fail. Each Lantaro answers a different part of play: social, combat, lore, healing, movement, carrying."],"Lantaro of Whispers":["information","Whispers secrets and legends, biased and in many languages. Information with a slant makes players weigh the source."],"Lantaro of Life":["composition","The Life orb heals 1 HP or stabilizes once a day and loves plants. The smallest effect in the family, delivered with the most personality."],"Lantaro of Flickering":["composition","Flickering teleports an ally 5 feet each round. A tiny reposition tool that can save a life at the right moment."],"Lantaro of Burden":["composition","Burden grapples or lifts on command once per combat. A helper with Strength 14 that sometimes takes things it shouldn't, so it creates scenes."],"Mask of Words":["freeform","Silence a creature and speak in their voice. A social weapon whose power is your script."],"Samuels Stupendous Suit":["freeform","Clothes that never stain. Zero mechanical power, all fantasy: the item's job is to make the player feel like Samuel."],"Halflings Scout Belt":["fixedness","Halflings turn invisible; bigger folk only lose their torso. The size rule turns a stealth item into a comedy prop for a tall character."],"Stein of Endless Ale":["freeform","Name the drink and who gets it. A tavern toy that helps a table play a scene."],"Aquara Helm":["fantasy","A water-filled helmet for aquatic races, sometimes used as a fish bowl. The joke admits the item's narrow use and makes it memorable."],"Archbakers Infinidough":["fixedness","Bread that expands to fill a room. It bridges a chasm, seals a tunnel or traps a monster: a food item solving a terrain problem."],"Donut of Holding":["tension","A food-only bag of holding that loses everything if you eat the whole donut. The risk is a joke waiting for a hungry player."],"Muffin of Death":["distortion","A muffin mimic that turns biters into muffins. It teaches players to distrust food in this world, a pattern break that lingers."],"Shoes of Not-So Brave":["inversion","Fear makes you fast and lets you drop and hide. Cowardice as a skill set."],"Jellydonut of Infinite Filling":["loop","Jam that gets harder to cross each round you spray it. The player chooses between spreading it wide and stacking one tile."],"Gloves and Sandals of Control":["versatility","Tiny immovable rods in gloves and sandals let you climb the air. A clever reuse of a known item at a smaller scale."],"Oxygen Pebble":["inversion","Air bubbles that let you breathe underwater and suffocate water-breathers. Help and harm from the same effect, depending on who stands in it."],"Cloak of the Deep Wilds":["context","A cloak that becomes a bush. Strong in the woods, odd in a city, which keeps it tied to its terrain."],"Portal Potty":["fixedness","A toilet-seat portal. Brian makes a teleport memorable by making it absurd."],"Rogue's Haybale":["fixedness","A haybale for safe landings and hiding, a nod to a famous stealth game trope. Known tropes are cheap to teach."],"Wishseed":["freeform","A seed that becomes any plant you describe. A prompt for creativity whose value depends on the planter."],"Arthul's Frozen Throne":["power","A whole ice palace and frost breath. A campaign-scale reward that changes the map."],"Torturer's Hooks":["tension","Lockpicks that double as torture tools. The item forces a moral decision."],"Moneytree":["exploit","A pot that grows coins. Mentally playtest the loop: plant a platinum coin and the economy bends. The \"properly thanked\" clause is the DM's brake."],"Wildred's Wonderful Wagon":["freeform","A cozy wagon that is bigger inside, with music and a trade bonus. A home base on wheels: comfort is a reward too."],"Mound of 1 Million Ants":["composition","Ants by default, or bees, scarabs and spiders if soaked in honey, sand or poison. One item with recipe-driven variants, a crafting system in miniature."],"Pendant of Water Repulsion":["context","Walk through liquid as if it isn't there. Strong in water levels and against water hazards."],"Cloak of the Flapping Bird":["control","A cloak that glides and flaps upward. Flight with rules, so the player has to plan arcs."],"Thinskin Compass":["freeform","A compass that misleads you unless you thank it. The item has a personality that the players have to manage."],"Recycler":["fixedness","A bag that breaks objects into parts. Every object becomes raw material."],"Bell of Paranoia":["distortion","A bell that rings when enemies are near and hops away when found. A paranoia generator for enemies."],"Bauble of Explosives":["randomness","Firecrackers at random targets and a fireball after a minute. Chaos with a timer: throw it and run."],"Bauble of Light Inversion":["inversion","Darkness becomes daylight and daylight becomes darkness. A one-line inversion that changes the whole scene."],"Accordian of Echoes":["synergy","Spend charges to recast a spell next turn. Repetition doubles a bard's best spell, and the lullaby recharge rewards a cozy scene."],"Bauble of Cats":["distortion","5d20 feral cats. It changes the scene from a stealth problem to a noise problem, and the plan becomes the distraction."],"Bauble of Soup":["fixedness","A cauldron of boiling soup: a hazard, a meal or a peace offering."],"Ancenstral Charm":["freeform","A grumpy ancestor lends a skill. The relationship is the fun."],"Burden of Pain":["loop","Store the damage you take and drop it on a foe. The more you suffer, the harder it hits, a revenge engine."],"Helm of Extreme Bravery":["loop","+1 to saves per nearby enemy. The more surrounded you are, the braver you get."],"Vest of Healing":["synergy","Every heal you receive grows. A target for the party's healer, which shapes positioning."],"DoppleGolem":["freeform","A level-1 copy of a creature with its personality. A companion that mirrors someone, a story device."],"Door of Excessive Shutting":["distortion","A door that slams on everyone. A hazard you can place, and a joke you can repeat."],"Golemling":["freeform","A clingy construct child. An NPC that creates scenes by its needs."],"Sporting Slingstaff":["tension","Set a number of rounds, then hit with the sling for a bonus that grows with the delay. Patience is the skill being tested."],"Pipe of Illusions":["coop","Illusions only fellow smokers can see. A party-only channel for communication or deception."],"Pauldrons of Feedback":["counterplay","Every spellcaster near you takes damage. It makes casters pay to stand near you."],"Slimplate":["power","Splint mail with no stealth penalty and a Dex bonus. A quiet upgrade with a funny side effect."],"Infernal Heart":["tension","Constitution 18, but crits against you deal triple damage. A clear trade: more HP, a new weakness enemies can aim for."],"Lightning Stone":["synergy","A battery for other magic items, recharged by lightning. An item that makes your other items better."],"Inciting Dummy":["counterplay","A taunt dummy that soaks attacks. Tanking handed to an object, which frees the tank to do something else."],"Cloak of Images":["loop","Each spell makes mirror images, one fading per round. Casting is defense, so the caster wants to keep casting."],"Sandals of Momentum":["loop","Speed grows each round you dash, up to +60. Momentum as a mechanic: it rewards commitment."],"Vision of the Dead, can only use while dead. can fly, invisibility, incorp, etc":["protect","A mask usable only while dead: you scout as a ghost while waiting for revival. A dead player still has a turn."],"Thundercage":["distortion","Shrinks creatures into a cage where they fight to the end. A trap and an arena in one object."],"Bauble of Snap Traps":["counterplay","Nine snap traps around a tile. Area denial: enemies have to choose a path."],"Balloon of Limited Freedom":["fixedness","A balloon that lifts its target forever. A removal tool written as a children's toy."],"Gravity Cube":["control","A vacuum that pulls everything within 50 feet. It reshapes positions for a minute."],"Orb of Mass Destruction":["loop","An orb that grows by eating objects and creatures. A snowball, literally."],"Friendly Familiar":["protect","An owl that compliments you and gives Perception and darkvision. A supportive friend who also does a job."],"Orangebeards Useful Keg":["fixedness","Turn anything into ale that tastes like it. A party trick with a dark side."],"Radiant Sheath":["power","Rest the weapon an hour, draw it with an element. A simple pre-fight ritual."],"Swordbreaker Gauntlet":["counterplay","Take the hit to break their weapon. A deliberate sacrifice that changes the fight."],"Spelleater Gloves":["counterplay","Counterspell, then keep the spell for an hour. The longer the cooldown, the bigger the spell you ate."],"Conductors Gloves":["versatility","Detachable hands with reach and flight. A strange verb that solves puzzles and grabs objects from afar."],"Amulet of Deception":["protect","Fake your death and go invisible. A reaction that turns a hit into an escape."],"Coin of Immense Value":["freeform","A coin that wants to be valued above 500 gold. The haggling becomes role-play with a coin that has opinions."]}};
